{"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"defaultPosition"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"_"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"position"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI9UnitPointV","text":"UnitPoint"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Scene","text":"Scene","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI5SceneP"},{"kind":"text","text":"\n"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"parameters":[{"name":"position","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" that specifies where to place a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"newly opened window relative to the screen bounds."}]}]}],"kind":"parameters"},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"return-value","type":"heading","text":"Return Value"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A scene that uses a default position for new windows.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The first time your app opens a window from a particular scene"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"declaration, the system places the window at the center of the screen by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"default. For scene types that support multiple simultaneous windows, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"system offsets each additional window by a small amount to avoid"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"completely obscuring existing windows."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You can override the default placement of the first window by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"applying a scene modifier that indicates where to place the window","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"relative to the screen bounds. For example, you can request that the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"system place a new window in the bottom trailing corner of the screen:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["@main","struct MyApp: App {","    var body: some Scene {","        WindowGroup {","            ContentView()","        }","        .defaultPosition(.bottomTrailing)","    }","}"],"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The system aligns the point in the window that corresponds to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"specified ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint"},{"text":" with the point in the screen that corresponds","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to the same unit point.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You typically use one of the predefined unit points — like","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint\/bottomTrailing","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" in the above example — but","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"you can also use a custom unit point. For example, the following","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"modifier aligns the point that’s one quarter of the way from the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"leading edge of the window with the point that’s one quarter of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the way from the leading edge of the screen, while centering the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"window in the y-dimension:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["WindowGroup {","    ContentView()","}",".defaultPosition(UnitPoint(x: 0.25, y: 0.5))"],"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The modifier affects any scene type that creates windows in macOS,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"namely:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/WindowGroup","type":"reference"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Window","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"DocumentGroup","type":"codeVoice"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Settings","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The value that you provide acts only as an initial default. During state"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"restoration, the system restores the window to the position that it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"last occupied."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/openswiftui\/swift\/never\/defaultposition(_:)"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Swift\/Never\/defaultPosition(_:)"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Swift","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Swift\/Never"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"Sets a default position for a window.","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"metadata":{"extendedModule":"OpenSwiftUI","role":"symbol